# ER040 Normalized Capture — Coherent Multi-Paper Series Audit 2

## Receipt status

Complete substantive capture of the second received publication-strategy audit. ER040 endorses a coherent multi-paper series or monograph, rejects destructive compression into one-to-three journal articles, interprets the minimum-paper rule as constrained by publishable length, proof integrity, audience, reproducibility, and full-content retention, and endorses the corrected five-assured-paper architecture with conditional Papers 6–7 and later gated domain papers.

## Main recommendations

1. Paper 1 introduces the canonical equation/schema and general architecture.
2. Paper 2 carries the theorem atlas, proofs, counterexamples, viability, and noncompensation.
3. Papers 3–5 separate accounting/diagnostics, nonlinear delay dynamics, and sampled governance/identification.
4. A021 becomes Paper 6 after certificate/coupling gates close.
5. Stage/spatial work becomes Paper 7 only after independent contribution gates.
6. Use a monograph/full technical report and living controlling architecture to preserve the complete corpus.
7. Avoid a mega-supplement and count genuinely independent results as papers.